  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, devices, and history for vague computer issue ticket"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Check laptop health for any obvious warnings related to the recurring issue"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is acting up again! I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail to work out what \"the thing\" is. Could you tell me:\n1. What happens? For example, is it slow, freezing, crashing or showing a blue screen, not turning on, showing an error message (if so, what does it say), or having trouble with Wi-Fi, printing or a particular app?\n2. When did it start this time, and roughly how often does it happen?\n3. Did it start after an update or after installing something new?\n4. When did you last fully restart the laptop (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid)?\n5. If you had a ticket about this before, do you remember roughly when, or the ticket number?\n\nOne more thing: our system shows your laptop hasn't connected to the company network for about 12 days. If it's been off, asleep, or not connected to Wi-Fi or VPN in that time, please let me know. That could be related.\n\nIn the meantime, a full restart often helps. A screenshot or photo of any error message would also be very useful. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "The ticket is too vague to diagnose (\"my computer is doing the thing again\"). User: Sofia Rossi (user_id 7, Marketing), account active, no failed sign-ins, not blocked. Her only device is BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11 Pro). Device status: offline, last check-in 2026-09-29, warning \"No check-in for 12 days\". Disk is healthy (54.7% free, 140 of 256 GB), so low disk space (KB-017) is ruled out. The user says this has happened before, so it's worth checking for earlier tickets from her. I've asked for symptoms, timing, recent changes, when she last restarted, and whether the laptop has been offline. If she describes slowness or freezing, follow KB-019. If she reports blue screens or repeated crashes, escalate per KB-019. The 12-day missed check-in may also need a look (device off, network/VPN problem, or management agent issue).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
